  { sku:'VOI-L06', title:'Live It Twice', subtitle:'The 7 Laws of Living the Second Time', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['longform','life','philosophy','it-twice'], blurb:'It-Twice Trilogy #3. Seven laws for living the second time — awake, on purpose — across five thresholds. The count is seven; the eighth is yours. The closer of the trilogy.', coverColor:'#9a4a2e', badge:'It-Twice · Book Three', promoPage:'/live/', paperback:15.99 , priceNG:12500, promoPageNG:'/live/', priceUSD:20, price:17 },
  { sku:'VOI-L07', title:'The Alibi of the Mind', subtitle:'A Field Manual for the Lies Your Intelligence Tells You', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['longform','mind','self-inquiry','flagship'], blurb:'Your mind does not lie loudly; it lies reasonably — with evidence, precedent, and a calm voice. Twenty-nine chapters on the respectable excuses and sophisticated avoidances intelligence builds for itself. Bring a pen.', coverColor:'#374151', featured:true, badge:'Longform · Field Manual', promoPage:'/alibi/', paperback:16.99 , priceNG:15000, promoPageNG:'/alibi/', priceUSD:20, price:17 },
  { sku:'VOI-L08', title:'Nothing to Understand, Everything to Know', subtitle:'The Complete Four-Book Novel', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['novel','fiction','longform','flagship'], blurb:'The estate’s only novel — three lives across four interlocking books and ninety-one chapters, colliding with the questions the nonfiction catalog keeps circling. Complete; no cliffhanger tax.', coverColor:'#3b1630', featured:true, badge:'A novel', promoPage:'/nothing/', paperback:22.99, pages:387 , priceNG:15000, promoPageNG:'/nothing/', priceUSD:20, price:17 },
  { sku:'VOI-L09', title:'Who Is God?', subtitle:'An Inquiry', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['faith','inquiry','spirituality','flagship'], blurb:'The estate’s central inquiry into the question every other title quietly stands next to. Written as an inquiry rather than a verdict — walking arguments, experiences, and silences from an Igbo centre, without forcing a conclusion and without surrendering judgement.', coverColor:'#0f4c4c', featured:true, badge:'The big inquiry', promoPage:'/god/', pages:354, hubRefs:22 , priceNG:18000, promoPageNG:'/god/', priceUSD:38, price:32 },
  { sku:'VOI-L10', title:'Why Must We Die?', subtitle:'104,000 Words on Mortality', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['death','philosophy','flagship'], blurb:'The volume the companions orbit: why the fact of death organizes everything humans build, believe, and buy. The estate’s deepest work on mortality, written with the same Igbo centre.', coverColor:'#2b2320', featured:true, badge:'The mortality flagship', promoPage:'/whydie/', pages:354 , priceNG:18000, promoPageNG:'/whydie/', priceUSD:38, price:32 },
  { sku:'VOI-L11', title:'The 3 A.M. Question', subtitle:'A 7-Day Field Guide to Quiet the Thought So You Can Sleep', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['death','sleep','inquiry','companion'], blurb:'The companion to Why Must We Die? for the reader the big book wakes up: a seven-day field guide for the 3am version of the question — the sleepless one, the one that arrives uninvited.', coverColor:'#2d1b4e', badge:'7-day companion', promoPage:'/3am/', pages:120 , priceNG:7500, promoPageNG:'/3am/', priceUSD:12, price:10 },
  { sku:'VOI-L12', title:'Good Death, Bad Death', subtitle:'How Igbos Judge a Death — A 20-Minute Read', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['death','igbo','culture','companion'], blurb:'The traditional Igbo ledger for judging a death — what makes one good and one bad, and what that ledger asks of a modern family planning or grieving today. Twenty honest minutes.', coverColor:'#8b4a1c', badge:'20 minutes', promoPage:'/gooddeath/', pages:104 , priceNG:7500, promoPageNG:'/gooddeath/', priceUSD:12, price:10 },
  { sku:'VOI-L13', title:'Death Was Never The Problem', subtitle:'How a Billion Africans Learned to Die Well', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['death','africa','culture'], blurb:'The $60-billion anti-death industry has a thesis; a billion Africans have an older, tested one. Eighteen chapters across four parts — Bryan Johnson, his father’s hospital death, the Igbo five-chapter framework, six lines in the sand. ~48,000 words.', coverColor:'#8a4a22', featured:true, badge:'Death · Book Three', promoPage:'/deathproblem/', pages:83 , priceNG:12500, promoPageNG:'/deathproblem/', priceUSD:20, price:17 },
  { sku:'VOI-L14', title:'What Are You Paying For?', subtitle:'Tithe, Offering, Sacrifice, Zakat — and the Courage to Give Without Fear', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['faith','spirituality','money'], blurb:'A church may need money; a shrine may need money. None of that settles what money does when it enters. Seven parts, thirty-five chapters, five appendices — landing on the courage to give without fear. ~40,000 words.', coverColor:'#5a3a1a', badge:'Faith · Book Two', promoPage:'/payingfor/', pages:71 , priceNG:12500, promoPageNG:'/payingfor/', priceUSD:20, price:17 },
  { sku:'VOI-L15', title:'Before You Leave', subtitle:'For Africans Deconstructing Faith and Reclaiming Their Roots', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['faith','deconstruction','africa','companion'], blurb:'You were not born with a religion; you were born into a story — and one day the story stops answering. Three movements, thirteen prompts, an evidence-status test. The companion for the reader leaving or re-examining inherited faith.', coverColor:'#4a4728', badge:'Faith · Companion', promoPage:'/beforeyouleave/', pages:75 , priceNG:7500, promoPageNG:'/beforeyouleave/', priceUSD:12, price:10 },
  { sku:'VOI-L16', title:'Somebody Called You', subtitle:'Spiritual Awakening Is Not an Experience — It Is Work', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['spirituality','awakening','calling','flagship'], blurb:'A call arrives. Consent turns it into a commission. The commission is a body of work that must outlive you. Four parts, fourteen chapters, written from inside an Igbo Christian life that refuses to fake synthesis.', coverColor:'#312e81', featured:true, badge:'Bestseller', promoPage:'/called/', priceNG:15000, promoPageNG:'/called/', priceUSD:20, price:17 },
  { sku:'VOI-L17', title:'The Ancestor You Are Becoming', subtitle:'You Are Not Healing Your Bloodline — You Are Starting One', author:'Munachimso Nwagbara',  shelf:'longform', tags:['lineage','spirituality','africa','flagship'], blurb:'A god is not sent. A god is started. Seven movements on Ime Agwu and Iru Agwu — what it costs, what you plant, what your children will keep. Written from inside the preparation, not from above it.', coverColor:'#7c2d12', featured:true, promoPage:'/ancestor/', priceNG:15000, promoPageNG:'/ancestor/', priceUSD:20, price:17 }
